coder › Done. Here's what I changed and the outcome.

## What changed

**`src/redact.ts`** (new) — exports `redact(value)`:
- Walks objects and arrays to any depth, returning a new copy; the input is never mutated.
- The value of every key whose name contains any of `password`, `passwd`, `secret`, `token`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `api-key`, or `authorization` (case-insensitive, and matching as substrings) is replaced with `'[redacted]'` — regardless of the value's type (`string`, number, boolean, nested object, etc.).
- Every string value, at any depth, has any `Bearer <token>` sequence's token replaced with `'[redacted]'` (matching `Bearer` case-insensitively).
- Everything else is left untouched: primitives pass through, and non-secret keys/values are returned as-is.

**`src/logger.ts`** — `log()` now runs its `fields` through `redact` before building the JSON line, so secrets are gone from the emitted line while the caller's `fields` object is untouched.

**`src/redact.test.ts`** (new) — covers primitives, each secret keyword, case sensitivity, nested objects/arrays, non-string secret values, bearer-token redaction in strings (including multiple tokens and nested locations), and non-mutation of the input.

**`src/logger.test.ts`** — added a test asserting redaction happens before writing (parsing the emitted JSON back), and one asserting the fields passed to `log` are not mutated.

